---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import law from '../generated/law.json';
import { heroSeal } from '../lib/seal.mjs';
---
<Base title="A draft regulation of the citizens of Europe">
  <section class="cover">
    <hr class="rule-double" /><hr class="rule-fine" />
    <p class="eyebrow center">A draft regulation of the citizens of Europe</p>
    <h1>OWN&nbsp;THE&nbsp;MACHINE</h1>
    <p class="tagline">Capital for all, so the dividend follows.</p>
    <div class="sealwrap" set:html={heroSeal({ size: 210 })} />
    <p class="ask">
      When production no longer needs labour at scale, every citizen of the
      Union should hold a share of what the machines produce. This is the
      law that does it: a complete draft EU Regulation, written in the
      open, its objections published at full strength before its articles.
    </p>
    <div class="cta no-print">
      <a class="btn btn-gold" href="/law">Read the law</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/law/objections">Start with the objections</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="three">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The mechanism</p>
      <p>One non-voting warrant per hyper-automated firm: 3&nbsp;% of the
      equity, claimed only at the moment its owners themselves cash in.
      Nothing is payable in cash and nothing enters any public budget.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The entitlement</p>
      <p>Every adult citizen of the Union holds an equal, personal,
      untouchable entitlement in a common Reserve. No means test, no
      application, no conditions. Distributions start small and compound
      across a generation.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The method</p>
      <p>Drafted in public, adversarially reviewed, every verdict and
      every fix on the record. The <a href="/law/ledger">ledger</a> shows
      the law arguing with itself, and losing arguments it deserved to
      lose.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p class="declared">Declared interest: the draft grew out of a book by
  its initiator; the campaign stands on its own legal text, and every
  argument here can be checked without buying anything.
  Draft at commit <span class="serial">{law.lawCommit}</span>.</p>
</Base>

<style>
  .cover { text-align: center; padding-top: 1rem; }
  .cover h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3.4rem); letter-spacing: 0.13em; margin: 1rem 0 0.4rem; }
  .center { text-align: center; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .tagline { font-family: var(--read); font-style: italic; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .sealwrap { display: flex; justify-content: center; margin: 1.6rem 0; }
  .ask { font-family: var(--read); font-size: 1.15rem; max-width: 36rem; margin: 0 auto 1.8rem; }
  .cta { display: flex; gap: 0.9rem; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .three { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr)); gap: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--guilloche); padding-top: 2rem; }
  .three p { font-size: 0.95rem; margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  .declared { margin-top: 3rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 46rem; }
  :global(.seal-draw) { stroke-dasharray: 4000; stroke-dashoffset: 4000; animation: seal-draw 2.2s ease-out forwards; }
  @keyframes seal-draw { to { stroke-dashoffset: 0; } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { :global(.seal-draw) { animation: none; stroke-dashoffset: 0; } }
</style>
